<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Clytia hemisphaerica Schnakenberg wavelength at 8.64 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 75.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics with Du = 1 µm²/s and Dv/Du = 20, and γ is already pinned near 2.227 s⁻¹ so k_* sits on 8.64 µm. The growth-rate comparison used an activator-only kick fit from t = 0. That probe is off the unstable eigenspace: Pearson r = 0.506 against Jacobian σ(k), which fails the 0.98 gate. The planula render and the equal-diffusion integrator exist in the file but were not yet the reported morphometric table. Holocene age is 0 Ma; the chronoseries is 1/1. Overall 75.8/100 (faithfulness 71.9, reproducibility 84.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit bd8176806dee28731b94a3866aa6609c1d9d4ba2; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 60, Morphometric validation 64, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-clytia-hemisphaerica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at bd8176806dee28731b94a3866aa6609c1d9d4ba2, image/png, 447751 B, 1152×1008 px, artifact_sha256 20a127f4c984202283143dd15af9c005b7459b523f6947cd6a1c370e6c527f83 (sha256 20a127f4c984202283143dd15af9c005b7459b523f6947cd6a1c370e6c527f83), spec_fingerprint 96a665cf0d7c09f92284588fc71976c4d562666ee4ba1270067ce2e4f5d4c878. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 96a665cf0d7c09f92284588fc71976c4d562666ee4ba1270067ce2e4f5d4c878; artifact_sha256: 20a127f4c984202283143dd15af9c005b7459b523f6947cd6a1c370e6c527f83; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/clytia_hemisphaerica_specimen.jpg=95bffe69b1854823..., datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=8e95bb9584ac6852..., datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=045903087c0ddff1..., datasets/clytia_hemisphaerica_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=014d315226f357c5...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing dispersion and Schnakenberg kinetics | Clytia hemisphaerica planula and medusa life cycle | Gonad opsin and hydrozoan pigment-cup ocelli as anatomical context; reconstructed_in_script: γ chosen so the most-unstable mode is the assigned 8.64 µm detail length | Planula mask used as the render domain; transfer_boundary: 8.64 µm is the MorphoEval detail anchor, not a published ocellus measurement; does_not_claim: A fossil wavelength shift (series length 1, age delta 0 Ma) | That the Pass-1 transient probe validates the dispersion relation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Put the equal-diffusion ablation (Dv = Du) in the measurement table next to the wild-type std(u).",
        "remediation needed: Refit σ from the analytic unstable eigenvector on the second half of each Fourier trajectory, and require Pearson r > 0.98 against the discrete-Laplacian dispersion.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the Momose planula and report aspect ratio, circularity, and an interior KS statistic whose value is not equal to its reference.",
        "remediation needed: Sweep Dv/Du at fixed γ and record that the selected wavelength moves monotonically." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.58e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

